2026-08-27  ICBR RC-wise susceptibility: low-denominator cells

WHAT I DID
Parsed all six pathogen sheets of ICBR_RC_Wise_Susceptibility__2_.xlsx
and listed every cell with fewer than 10 isolates tested.
Output: ICBR_low_N_cells.xlsx

RESULT
3,276 cells total. 260 have N < 10 and are excluded.

DECISIONS
- Exclude the individual cell where N < 10. Keep the centre, year and
  pathogen otherwise.
  Reason: excluding whole centres would systematically remove newer
  centres, which are mostly in under-represented regions.
- N is the denominator printed inside the cell (isolates tested against
  that antibiotic at that centre), not the column-header N, which is
  the national total for the year.

LIMITATION
Low-N cells cluster in smaller centres (RIMS Imphal, Apollo Chennai,
Artemis Gurugram) and rarer organisms (P. mirabilis, E. cloacae).
Exclusion therefore thins the northeast more than Maharashtra or Delhi.

OPEN
RC number to institution key is published only in the 2021 report
(Figure (i), p.5). Institution names for other years are provisional.


2026-08-29 Metagenome Metadata Parsing from NCBI SRA and ENA

WHAT I DID
Parsed NCBI and ENA databases for metagenomes using SRA Advanced Search with results then sent to SRA Run Selector and ENA Advanced Search. 
ENA Advanced Search Query: Data Type - Raw Reads. country="India" AND library_strategy="wgs" AND instrument_platform="illumina" AND first_public>2010-01-01 AND first_public<2026-06-01
Fields Included: run_accession, sample_accession, experiment_title, country, library_strategy, center_name, location, collection_date, first_public, tax_id, lat, lon, scientific_name. 

NCBI SRA Advanced Search Query: "India"[All Fields] AND "METAGENOMIC"[Source] AND "WGS"[Strategy] AND "ILLUMINA"[Platform] AND ("2010/01/01"[PDAT] : "2026/06/01"[PDAT]).
Prior to sending runs that satisfy the queries to Run Selector to download the metadata, runs were filtered using the NCBI taxonomy IDs 408170 and 527639 for human gut metagenomes and wastewater metagenomes respectively.
RESULT
Output: ENA Advanced Search 2.tsv, 46683 runs parsed. 
Output: Human Gut Metagenome Run Selector SRA.csv, 7774 runs parsed; Wastewater Metagenome Run Selector SRA.csv, 3601 runs parsed.

Decisions
DDBJ runs were omitted because runs are shared between NCBI SRA, ENA and DDBJ daily and tests of merging all three databases into a single dataframe of metagenome samples yield zero extra samples compared to merging just NCBI SRA and ENA. DDBJ search did not have consistent or detailed enough properties in fields to identify runs that fit the query criteria.   

